+# VXP-Core v0.8.8.4 — ARM/Lua Hot-Block Fast Path
+
+## Goal
+
+Optimize ARM-heavy Lua VXP workloads without changing guest work, timer cadence, framebuffer semantics, callback limits, or security boundaries.
+
+Target used for validation:
+
+- file: `Chetaslua(1).vxp`
+- size: 516,132 bytes
+- SHA-256: `9e7ce08d33f5f6caccf446a1ca6db4ee91c39eacd38b05f0fbf234b9cb041b85`
+- backend: ELF_ARM / ARM EABI5 PIE
+
+The target binary is not included in the repository or release package.
+
+## Profile-driven implementation
+
+v0.8.8.4 extends the v0.8.8.3 cached execution architecture to the ARM-heavy paths exercised by the embedded Lua VM:
+
+- JIT-friendly cached ARM dispatcher rather than re-entering the monolithic ARM decoder for every cached instruction;
+- separate LDM/STM block-transfer decode kinds and compact helpers;
+- word LDR/STR split by immediate/register offset and load/store direction;
+- specialized hot ADD and MOV data-processing paths;
+- generic cached single-data/data-processing fallbacks for remaining valid families;
+- full decoder retained for rare/overlapping families, tracing, single-step and compatibility fallback;
+- executable-write invalidation and block termination semantics preserved.
+
+Rejected prior experiments remain rejected: larger 16-instruction blocks and a secondary GuestMemory data MRU did not produce stable median gains.
+
+## Same-host fixed-work A/B validation — 2026-09-21
+
+JVM: OpenJDK 21, `-Xms512m -Xmx512m`. Six trials per side; trial 0 excluded by the benchmark median. Workload stops at exactly 40 framebuffer frames.
+
+Exact semantic signature on every measured run:
+
+`40 frames / 205,398,835 instructions / 39 events / 37 timers / timeout=false`
+
+| Metric | v0.8.8.3 | v0.8.8.4 ARM/Lua | Delta |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| warm median MIPS | 49.097 | **63.389** | **+29.11%** |
+| warm median 40-frame wall time | 4183.567 ms | **3240.267 ms** | **-22.55%** |
+| fixed-work equivalent FPS | 9.561 | **12.345** | **+29.12%** |
+| guest instructions | 205,398,835 | 205,398,835 | exact |
+| frames | 40 | 40 | exact |
+| events | 39 | 39 | exact |
+| timer callbacks | 37 | 37 | exact |
+
+The release criterion is median improvement with an identical work signature, not a single best trial.
+
+## Continuous performance gate
+
+The repository-level `scripts/perf_gate.py` and `.github/workflows/continuous-performance.yml` pin this title by SHA-256, warm the runtime before measurement, aggregate repeated runs and reject configurable FPS regression. The fixed-frame A/B gate in this source package additionally compares baseline and candidate JARs under identical guest work.
+
+## Result
+
+v0.8.8.4 is accepted as an ARM/Lua hot-block performance release only because it improves the measured fixed-work FPS while preserving the exact guest-work signature. No timer-speed hack or gameplay acceleration is used.
